# The floor raised from the leaf's entry alone, as member 1 first shipped it. A
# clear deletes the epoch row, so epoch values recur. A pre-purge duplicate that
# wrote the row but not yet its entry at this partition finds the floor below its
# epoch, writes the entry after the purge and appends; the re-created incarnation
# claims the same epoch, is admitted as AlreadyDurable, and arms past the
# duplicate's appends (#5641).
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestFloorFromEntryOnly
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: retirement raises the floor to the leaf's entry only, not to its epoch row
PERTURBS: Recreate
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ retired' = Max2(retired, Max2(fence, rowEpoch))
    /\ lRetired' = Max2(lRetired, Max2(fence, rowEpoch))
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the floor is built from the entry alone.
    /\ retired' = Max2(retired, fence)
    /\ lRetired' = Max2(lRetired, fence)
--- END